<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Sint Maarten</h1><p class="st-meta">2010 CE – present · capital Philipsburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Southern half of a small island shared with France since 1648, a country within the Kingdom of the Netherlands since 2010.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Sint Maarten was part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/netherlands-antilles">Netherlands Antilles</a> until that country was dissolved on 10 October 2010. Islanders had voted in 2000 for separate status, and it became an autonomous country within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarah-wescot-williams">Sarah Wescot-Williams</a> as first prime minister. The island's division with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/collectivity-of-saint-martin">French Saint-Martin</a> dates from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-concordia">Treaty of Concordia</a> of 1648.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Sint Maarten has its own parliament, government and constitution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philipsburg">Philipsburg</a>, while the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> oversees defence, foreign affairs and, through a board, public finances. Its economy depends on tourism, especially cruise ships and visitors flying in to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princess-juliana-international-airport">Princess Juliana Airport</a>. English is the everyday language, and much of the population is of migrant origin. Governments have been unstable, with frequent changes of prime minister.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-irma">Hurricane Irma</a> devastated the island in 2017, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> reconstruction aid came with conditions on governance. Sint Maarten remains a country within the kingdom, debating its relationship with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-hague">The Hague</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sint-maarten.jpg" alt="Sint Maarten" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Shervinafshar, based on work of Washiucho. Earlier non-PD versions by SiBr4, Fry1989, and An... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sint_Maarten.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>2010 CE – present</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Philipsburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sarah Wescot-Williams, Silveria Jacobs</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/sint-maarten">Sint Maarten</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Country of Sint Maarten</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2018&amp;focus=sint-maarten" aria-label="Sint Maarten on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="2970 1509 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sint Maarten lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3290 1765L5110 626M3290 1765L3106 1982"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5110 626h0M3106 1982h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3290 1765h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3290 1765h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Philipsburg. <a href="/atlas?year=2018&amp;focus=sint-maarten">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
